-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Finders Keepers
  Publisher   Mastertronic, 1985
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Finders Keepers (1985)(Mastertronic)[Magic Knight 1].z80
  MD5         0244e9b61aa18d6a9f1e77d102da1ea9

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Changes     1.1: Starts with the Next's DivMMC automap switched off:
              NextZXOS leaves it on, and on current cores that could crash the
              game or spoil its drawing

  Note        Keys: 8 on the menu to play; M right, N left, SPACE to jump, X
              and the other keys the game lists for its commands. The Magic
              Knight and the creatures are Next sprites over their own pixels,
              in their own colours, so they no longer colour the scenery they
              pass; the rooms, the panel and the few figures the game draws in
              whole coloured cells (the spinning axe on cyan, the blacked-out
              dragons) stay as the game draws them.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite strength

  Checked against this release's code: 34169 is the first byte of the routine
  that takes strength when a creature touches the Knight; a RET there skips it
  (in a free run, strength stays at 72). Not played.

