-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      NexClash differential verification against four machine-played
              recordings; run from its menu in OverSpec; Tang FPGA board:
              loads and plays. Not played by a person.

  Replay      IDENTICAL on 4 machine-played recordings, 52,127 frames (three
              exploring runs from the start, and one segment for each of the
              castle's 22 rooms and the ending, entered by the game's own
              start-of-life code with the room number poked): at every hook
              original and patched code from the same state to a common resume
              point (every register but R, all memory but the attribute cells
              the original's painter colours), every figure's XOR pixels
              against its sprite at every main loop pass (16.3 million sprite
              pixels), the painter skipped for every sprite figure and run as
              the original for the rest; 6,912 unit cases (every colour and
              mask kind, frame and edge position) pass; 8 of 8 negative
              controls detected

  Emulator    OverSpec, from the patch menu: Infinite strength on, the game's
              menu, the King's Palace and the Castle Teleport Room reached
              with the creatures as sprites

  Coverage    Machine-played recordings only: rooms 0-21 and the ending by
              poked room number, three exploring runs (2 to 4 rooms each by
              walking), creatures, strength loss, the teleport, command
              windows; not reached by play: trading, the full quest and the
              escape

  Hardware    Tang Nano 20K FPGA build of the Next, with DivMMC automap on and
              124 sprites left visible by a previous program: loads, plays
              through three rooms, no crash

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
